# {{senseid|en|middle}} [[middle|Middle]] or centre in location/position.
#: {{uxi|en|[[Mesoamerica|Mesoamerica]]}} is a pre-Columbian cultural region extending from the southern part of Mexico to an area that comprises some parts of the countries of Central America, {{uxi|en|[[mesohepatectomy|'''meso'''hepatectomy]]}} is the surgical removal of the middle part of the liver, {{uxi|en|[[mesoscaphe|'''meso'''scaphe]]}} is a submersible submarine designed for drifting on sea currents in the middle depth layers of the ocean
# {{senseid|en|mesoscale}} Between a ''macro-'' scale and ''micro-'' scale in scope or analysis.
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesoeconomics|'''meso'''economics]]}} is economics on a scale between that of microeconomics and macroeconomics, {{uxi|en|[[mesoevolution|'''meso'''evolution]]}} is evolutionary change on a time-scale intermediate between microevolution and macroevolution, {{uxi|en|[[mesometeorology|'''meso'''meteorology]]}} is the study of atmospheric phenomena on a larger scale than micrometeorology
# {{senseid|en|medium}} [[medium|Medium]] in size.
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesobrowser|'''meso'''browser]]}} is a medium-sized browser (animal that browses, {{uxi|en|[[mesocavern|'''meso'''cavern]]}} is a medium-sized cave, cavern or similar void, {{uxi|en|[[mesohabitat|'''meso'''habitat]]}} is a medium-sized habitat
# {{senseid|en|between}} [[between|Between]].
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesochannel|'''meso'''channel]]}} is a channel, between two others, used as a heat exchanger, {{uxi|en|[[mesoclitic|'''meso'''clitic]]}} is a clitic inserted inside a word (such as between a stem and a suffix), {{uxi|en|[[mesolayer|'''meso'''layer]]}} is a layer that exists between others
# {{senseid|en|intermediate}} [[intermediate|Intermediate]] between two properties or characteristics.
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesocratic|'''meso'''cratic]]}} is having a more or less even mixture of light and dark constituents, {{uxi|en|[[mesognathous|'''meso'''gnathous]]}} is having the jaws between prognathous and orthognathous, {{uxi|en|[[mesohydrophyte|'''meso'''hydrophyte]]}} is any plant whose tolerance to moisture is intermediate between that of a mesophyte and a hydrophyte.
# {{senseid|en|mesentery}} {{lb|en|anatomy}} Referring to the [[mesentery]].
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesoappendix|'''meso'''appendix]]}} is part of the mesentery found near the appendix and the terminal ileum, {{uxi|en|[[mesoduodenum|'''meso'''duodenum]]}} is the mesentery of the duodenum, {{uxi|en|[[mesogastrium|'''meso'''gastrium]]}} is the part of the embryonic mesentery that includes the stomach
# {{senseid|en|mesial}} {{lb|en|anatomy}} [[mesial|Mesial]] in location, position, or direction: towards the midline of the body.
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesoanterior|'''meso'''anterior]]}} is mesial and anterior, {{uxi|en|[[mesomedial|'''meso'''medial]]}} is mesial and medial, {{uxi|en|[[meson|'''meso'''n]]}} is the mesial plane dividing the body into similar right and left halves
# {{senseid|en|normal}} [[normal|Normal]], [[average]], or [[typical]].
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesochronic|'''meso'''chronic]]}} is based upon time averages of observed phenomena, {{uxi|en|[[mesocrystal|'''meso'''crystal]]}} is an ordered aggregate of similarly-sized crystals, {{uxi|en|[[mesokurtosis|'''meso'''kurtosis]]}} is the property of having kurtosis equal to that of a normal distribution; equivalently, having zero excess kurtosis
# {{senseid|en|forward}} {{lb|en|dentistry}} The [[forward]] side of a tooth.
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesocone|'''meso'''cone]]}} is a conule in the median mure where the mesoloph is attached to it, {{uxi|en|[[mesoflexus|'''meso'''flexus]]}} is a flexus between the mesoloph and the paracone, {{uxi|en|[[mesoloph|'''meso'''loph]]}} is a crest in front of the metaflexus, connected to the median mure
# {{senseid|en|midtime}} The middle of a time period, or medium in duration.
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesocenozoic|'''meso'''cenozoic]]}} is relating to the middle of the Cenozoic era, {{uxi|en|[[mesocratic|'''meso'''cratic]]}} is relating to mesocracy, or rule by the middle class, {{uxi|en|[[Mesolithic|Mesolithic]]}} is of or referring to the Middle Stone Age (also the Mesolithic period or the Mesolithic age), a prehistoric period that lasted between 10000 and 3000 BC
# {{senseid|en|quasi}} [[quasi|Quasi]] or [[partial]].
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesocarnivore|'''meso'''carnivore]]}} is any animal whose diet consists of 30–70% meat, {{uxi|en|[[mesobilirubin|'''meso'''bilirubin]]}} is a reduced form of bilirubin that is the primary pigment of bile acid, {{uxi|en|[[mesoparasite|'''meso'''parasite]]}} is a parasitic copepod that lives partly embedded in its host
# {{senseid|en|moderate}} [[moderate|Moderate]], [[medium]] in [[quantity]].
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesoendemic|'''meso'''endemic]]}} is having some transmission in an area, {{uxi|en|[[mesoeutrophic|'''meso'''eutrophic]]}} is having a medium amount of nutrients and minerals, {{uxi|en|[[mesohaline|'''meso'''haline]]}} is moderately salty; brackish
# {{senseid|en|chirality}}{{lb|en|chemistry}} Designating an [[achiral]] member of a group of [[diastereoisomer]]s that has at least one [[chiral]] member.
#: {{uxi|en|[[mesotartaric acid|'''meso'''-tartaric acid]]}}, {{uxi|en|[[mesolytic|'''meso'''lytic]]}}

